lief precedent): no second registry kind hears the same men (PR's `patrol_order`, with its own `sent · kept`, is withdrawn from PL's side, §15.12), and no second `service_refused` row prices the same men for the same call. A summons row is PL's OWN. PL mints it, with `episodeId` the call-in request's own key (its `warAnchorKey` and `askedTick`, WC §1.9.1 — the request record carries no id field of its own), so there is one row per member per call; no other volume requests it, and it carries no request prefix (§4.6). Where PL-5's summons is not built (WC-5 unlanded) or `polityObligationsEnabled` is dark, the crown summons no member's riders at all; the root's OWN riders still ride members' roads by the hold (§15.12).]
